13. Advanced Topics (Big Differentiator)

These topics separate mid-level developers from senior/architect-level engineers. Most real-world Salesforce scaling problems live here.

13.1 Performance Optimization

Performance issues in Salesforce are almost always due to:

Poor SOQL design
Inefficient Apex
Large data volumes
Bad UI rendering (LWC/Aura)
Query Optimization (SOQL)
Core Rule:

“Your query should return only what you need, as fast as possible.”

Key Techniques
1. Avoid SELECT *

Bad:

SELECT Id, Name, Description__c FROM Account

Good:

SELECT Id, Name FROM Account
2. Use WHERE Clauses Effectively

Bad:

SELECT Id FROM Account

Good:

SELECT Id FROM Account WHERE CreatedDate = LAST_N_DAYS:30
3. Avoid Non-Selective Queries (Critical in LDV)

Bad:

WHERE Status__c != 'Closed'

Good:

WHERE Status__c = 'Open'
4. Use Indexed Fields

Indexed fields:

Primary Keys (Id)
Foreign Keys
External IDs
Custom indexed fields
5. Use Query Plan Tool

Salesforce provides Query Plan Tool:

Shows cost
Shows selectivity
Helps optimize queries
Apex Optimization
Anti-pattern (Common mistake)
for(Account acc : accounts){
    List<Contact> cons = [SELECT Id FROM Contact WHERE AccountId = :acc.Id];
}
Optimized (Bulkified)
List<Contact> cons = [SELECT Id, AccountId FROM Contact WHERE AccountId IN :accountIds];
Key Principles
Bulkify everything
Avoid SOQL inside loops
Avoid DML inside loops
Use collections (Map, Set)
Caching

Caching reduces repeated computation and DB calls.

Types of Caching
1. Platform Cache
Org Cache
Session Cache

Use case:

Frequently accessed config
API responses
2. Custom Caching (Apex)
static Map<Id, Account> cacheMap;
3. Client-Side Cache (LWC)
@wire caching
Lightning Data Service
When to Use Caching
Expensive queries
Static data
Repeated API calls
13.2 Large Data Volume (LDV)

LDV = Millions of records

This is where most systems break if not designed properly.

Indexing
Types of Indexes
Type	Description
Standard Index	Default (Id, Name, Lookup)
Custom Index	Requested via Salesforce
External ID	Automatically indexed
When to Request Custom Index
Field used in WHERE clause frequently
High data volume object
Poor query performance
Selectivity (VERY IMPORTANT)

A query is selective if it filters enough data.

Salesforce Rule:
Standard Index → must return < 30% of records
Custom Index → must return < 10% of records
Example

Bad (Non-selective):

WHERE Status__c = 'Active'   // 80% records

Good (Selective):

WHERE Status__c = 'Active' AND Region__c = 'India'
LDV Best Practices
Use skinny tables (via Salesforce support)
Archive old data
Use async processing (Batch Apex)
Avoid full table scans
Partition data logically
13.3 Platform Events

This is Salesforce’s event-driven architecture backbone.

What are Platform Events?
Asynchronous message bus
Decouples systems
Works like Kafka-lite inside Salesforce
Architecture
Publisher → Event Bus → Subscriber
Use Cases
Microservices communication
Integration with external systems
Real-time updates
Order processing systems
Example
Event Definition
Order_Event__e event = new Order_Event__e(
    Order_Id__c = '123',
    Status__c = 'Created'
);
EventBus.publish(event);
Subscriber (Trigger)
trigger OrderEventTrigger on Order_Event__e (after insert) {
    for(Order_Event__e e : Trigger.New){
        System.debug(e.Status__c);
    }
}
Key Characteristics
Feature	Behavior
Async	Yes
Replay	Supported
Transaction	Separate
Scalability	High
When to Use Platform Events

Use when:

Loose coupling required
Async processing
Multiple consumers

Avoid when:

You need immediate response
Strict transaction control
13.4 Custom Metadata & Custom Settings

This is config-driven development — critical for scalable systems.

Why This Matters

Hardcoding = junior
Config-driven = architect

Custom Settings
Types
List Custom Settings
Hierarchy Custom Settings
Use Case
MySetting__c setting = MySetting__c.getInstance();
Limitations
Not deployable easily
Less flexible
Custom Metadata (IMPORTANT)

Modern replacement for Custom Settings.

Advantages
Deployable via packages
Version controlled
Queryable like objects
Example
SELECT MasterLabel, Value__c FROM Config__mdt
Real Use Cases
Use Case	Example
Feature Flags	Enable/disable logic
API Endpoints	Store URLs
Business Rules	Threshold values
Country Config	Tax rules
Pattern: Config-Driven Logic

Instead of:

if(country == 'India'){
    tax = 18;
}

Use:

SELECT Tax__c FROM Country_Config__mdt WHERE Country__c = 'India'
Final Architecture Insight

At scale, your system evolves like this:

Level	Approach
Beginner	Hardcoded logic
Intermediate	Some optimization
Advanced	Indexed + selective queries
Architect	Event-driven + config-driven + cached